<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mesalim of Kish</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 2600 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/27th-century-bce">27th century BCE</a> · Also known as Mesilim</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mesalim of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kish">Kish</a> was an Early Dynastic king of Kish who reigned around 2600 BCE and claimed authority over other Sumerian cities. Inscriptions from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lagash">Lagash</a> record that he arbitrated the border dispute between Lagash and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umma">Umma</a> over the Gu-edena plain and set up a boundary stone. His settlement did not hold, and the quarrel between the two cities lasted for generations.</p></div>
